  "ingredients": [
    "5 large egg (separated)",
    "1 cup almond flour",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "1/4 cup erythritol",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 teaspoon almond extract",
    "1/4 teaspoon liquid stevia",
    "1/2 teaspoon cream of tartar",
    "1/2 tablespoon lemon zest",
    "2 tablespoon olive oil",
    "4 tablespoon butter",
    "4 tablespoon heavy whipping cream",
    "1/3 cup raspberries",
    "1/2 tablespoon lemon zest"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 325F. Separate the eggs into two bowls. In a separate bowl, mix together all of the dry ingredients, except the cream of tartar.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8626.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk the egg yolks with vanilla, almond extract, and liquid stevia.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8630.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients until well combined and set aside for a moment.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8634.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Making sure beaters are clean and dry, whip the egg whites with the cream of tartar until stiff peaks form.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8638.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the lemon zest into the egg whites until well incorporated.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8641.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gently fold the egg whites into the dough, adding one-third at a time. Pour the batter into lightly oiled cupcake or cake molds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8645.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 25 minutes or until they've risen and a toothpick comes out clean. Once done, remove from the oven and let cool.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8654.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, melt the butter in a pan on the stovetop until lightly browned.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8655.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the heavy cream and raspberries and mix to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8680.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "As the mixture cooks, gently mash the raspberries and allow the sauce to reduce. Let cool.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/IMG_8683.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ice the cakes, sprinkle over the lemon zest, and serve!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/italian-lemon-sponge-cake/#wprm-recipe-51057-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/ItalianLemonSpongeCake.jpg"
    }
  ],
